I just completed my first ascension after only two weeks of playing
(I started Feb. 10). Yes, I was spoiled to hell by the wiki, I
watched a let's play on YouTube, I ascended with arguably the easiest
character, and all things considered, it was IMO a fairly lucky run.
Tyr was angry with me, but the RNG was on my side.

However, I know some more spoiled than I go years without an
ascension, so I'm still pretty excited. And the endgame was fairly
eventful, so I thought I'd share. First, the dumplog:

http://alt.org/nethack/userdata/k/kc/dumplog/1392893481.nh343.txt

Some notables:

* Dwarven Valkyrie was chosen randomly on accident. I meant to play a
  Chaotic Human (because peacefuls annoy me) Wizard. My best run 
  previously was as a Neutral Gnomish Wizard.

* Prior to this run, I had only completed one quest (the wizard's)
  and my deepest descent was Medusa's Isle (drowned by an eel).

* I found an early bones file. Interestingly, they were *my* bones...
  from *my last* run... On NAO... Not sure the odds of this happening,
  but this was extremely fortunate because I knew exactly what was in
  the pile, including speed boots and cloak of magic resistance.

* My typical early game strategy is to find a general store and an altar
  and trek between them to identify loot. In this run, however, the
  *only* random store was on DLVL 15, and the nearest altar was DLVL 3.
  This doesn't suit my style so I almost considered quitting at this
  point if not for the bones loot, so I took it to Minetown.

* The lighting store in Minetown had exactly 9 candles and nothing else,
  so I stashed those and went through most of the game without a light
  source. After a frustrating run of Gehennom without so much as a
  potion of oil, I decided to trek back to the mines and kill all the
  peacefuls, which yielded a magic lamp! I blessed it, but I never
  rubbed it. I had two wands of wishing by this point anyway.

* I found an early wand of wishing (0:2), but it sat in my stash until I
  finally found a scroll of identify, which wasn't until after Minetown
  and Sokoban and before the quest.

* My first wish was SDSM. At this point I had already identified scrolls
  of charging and genocide (both blessed), so I considered a magic
  marker, but decided to hold off in case one shows up. Eventually, I
  wished for two magic markers before finding a third.

* When Excalibur was the only artifact in play, I considered wishing
  for Grayswandir, but I assumed incorrectly that if I sacrificed for
  it, I'd be able to level it up to expert. My sacfest yielded Mjollnir,
  Frost Brand, and Werebane. With Werebane, I leveled my saber skill to
  basic before realizing that that's all I was going to get. So with my
  castle wand and 5 artifacts in play (including the Orb of Weight), I
  got Grayswandir in only two wishes. The whole sacfest was pointless.

* I destroyed my speed boots trying to fireproof them with scroll of
  destroy armor after my confusion wore off. With two wands of polymorph
  in hand, I backtracked to collect all the magical polyfodder strewn
  about in hopes of morphing new speed boots. My polyfest yielded just
  about every piece of magical armor, amulet, ring and item *except* the
  speed boots, but I found some eventually.

* I found two amulets of life saving before Vlad's Tower. While checking
  my inventory once, I realized the first one was gone. Wand of
  enlightenment confirmed that I was indeed saved, but I don't remember
  how or when.

* Gehennom was so tedious for me that I wanted to stop playing and
  considered doing a half-assed ascension run just to get it over with,
  not caring if I live or die, but even that didn't seem like much fun.
  So I took a break for a day and came back with renewed excitement
  about ascending. I knew that with my kit I had a fighting chance, and
  that with my stock of potions of object detection and cursed scrolls
  of teleport, I could loot Gehennom with less tedium and map it in the
  process. So I carefully completed my kit then wrote the scrolls
  necessary to supe up my gear.

Now on to the ascension run:

* The ascension started pretty well. After no mysterious force, hard
  enemies or Wizard for ~20 DLVLs, I was skeptical that I even had the
  real Amulet. I wrote a scroll of identify to confirm it, but I still
  wasn't convinced until The Plane of Earth.

* This is where my luck almost ran out. Literally one step into The
  Plane of Earth I find a large box. Stupidly, I open it. Electric
  trap! Ring of free action: gone! Ring of conflict: gone! Ring of
  levitation: gone! I figured that with only 5 more DLVLs, it's no big
  deal. I had no idea how essential those rings are to those levels.

* On The Plane of Air I was stuck and surrounded by dragons. I lost half
  my HP before I realized that I *need* a ring of levitation. So I
  pulled out my wand of wishing (1:2) and got one. After getting my butt
  kicked some more I realized a new ring of conflict would be nice, so
  that was my last wish. Barely made it out of there alive.

* On The Astral Plane is where I almost died again. I don't remember if
  it were the priests or the angels, but somebody kept paralyzing me. I
  really needed my ring of free action back, so I tried to wrest a final
  wish from my (1:0) wand. After two failed attempts, I realized that I
  wasn't going to find any safe place to do it. So in a last ditch
  attempt, I pulled a ring of hunger and potion of polymorph out of my
  bag and dipped the former in the latter. I don't know what the odds
  are, but it turned into a ring of free action!!! Had that not worked,
  I probably would have remembered that I had a magic lamp, but I'm glad
  it worked out this way because the feeling was awesome. So with free
  action on my finger, I beelined straight for the northernmost altar,
  which just happened to be that of Tyr, and sacrificed the Amulet.

So there you have it! I was doubtful, but the game is winnable even for
a noob if you play your cards right. I'll probably have to give it
another run to determine if it was a fluke or not, but I'll more than
likely take a break for a while. 

Anyway, good luck to everybody who's still descending and happy hacking!

